## Tech Stack Summary

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|-----------|
| Frontend framework | React 18 + Vite + TypeScript |
| State management | Zustand |
| UI components | Ant Design 5 |
| Calendar | React Big Calendar |
| Drag-and-drop | @hello-pangea/dnd (maintained DnD fork) |
| Charts | Recharts |
| Real-time | Socket.io-client |
| HTTP client | Axios |
| Backend framework | NestJS (TypeScript) |
| ORM | TypeORM |
| Database | PostgreSQL 15 |
| Auth | JWT + bcrypt + Passport.js |
| File upload | Multer |
| PDF export | pdf-lib |
| Discord | axios (webhook POSTs) |
| Containerization | Docker + docker-compose |

---

## Phased Roadmap

### Phase 1 — Foundation (Weeks 1–2)
- Project scaffolding, Docker setup
- PostgreSQL schema + migrations
- Auth system (login, JWT, RBAC middleware)
- Login page
- User management (Admin UI)

### Phase 2 — Scheduling & Inventory (Weeks 3–4)
- Schedule submission + calendar view
- Discord schedule posting
- Inventory table + add/edit + check-in/out logs

### Phase 3 — Tasks & Wishlists (Weeks 5–6)
- Kanban board (projects + tasks)
- Task Discord notifications
- Wishlist system + budget tracking
- Calendar integration for tasks

### Phase 4 — Dashboard & Reports (Weeks 7–8)
- Dashboard widgets (Gantt, pie, summary cards)
- Real-time via Socket.io
- Weekly report form (employee) + admin view
- PDF export of weekly reports
- Discord report reminders

### Phase 5 — Polish & Extras (Weeks 9–10)
- Audit trails
- File attachments everywhere
- Time tracking
- Mobile responsiveness
- Full test coverage

---

## Verification Plan

### Backend Unit & Integration Tests (Jest + Supertest)
```bash
cd backend
npm run test          # Unit tests for services
npm run test:e2e      # E2E API tests (supertest against real DB via test container)
```
Key test suites to write:
- `auth.e2e-spec.ts` — login success/fail, token refresh, role guards
- `schedules.e2e-spec.ts` — submit, retrieve, Discord post
- `tasks.e2e-spec.ts` — CRUD, RBAC restrictions
- `reports.e2e-spec.ts` — submit, PDF export byte length check

### Frontend Component Tests (Vitest + React Testing Library)
```bash
cd frontend
npm run test
```
- Login form renders and submits
- Protected routes redirect unauthenticated users
- Kanban columns render tasks correctly

### Browser E2E (Cypress)
```bash
cd frontend
npx cypress open   # Interactive
npx cypress run    # Headless CI
```
Key flows: login → dashboard, submit schedule, create task, submit report.

### Manual Verification
1. Run `docker-compose up` and navigate to `http://localhost:3000`.
2. Login as Admin user (seeded) — should redirect to Dashboard.
3. Login as Employee — should only see personal views, no Admin nav items.
4. Submit a schedule, go to Admin view, verify unified calendar populates.
5. Create a task assigned to Employee → verify Discord notification fires.
6. Employee submits weekly report → Admin exports PDF → verify PDF downloads.
